  <section id="quick-start-requirements" class="quick-start-section">
    <h2>1. Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Node.js 22+ or Bun installed.</li>
      <li>A TypeScript-compatible project.</li>
      <li>Access to the AVSS Lite GitHub repository.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="quick-start-install" class="quick-start-section">
    <h2>2. Install AVSS Lite</h2>
    <p>Install the package using Bun:</p>
    <CodeBlock language="bash" :code="'bun add github:Rakaa503/Avidev-Security'" />
  </section>

  <section id="quick-start-import" class="quick-start-section">
    <h2>3. Import the toolkit</h2>
    <p>Import the utilities from the package root.</p>
    <CodeBlock language="typescript" :code="`import { validate, validateOrThrow, logger, createSecurity } from 'avss-lite-Raka503';
import { z } from 'zod';`" />
  </section>

  <section id="quick-start-validation" class="quick-start-section">
    <h2>4. Validate input</h2>
    <p>
      AVSS Lite provides validate() for safe parsing and
      validateOrThrow() for exception-based validation.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock language="typescript" :code="`import { z } from 'zod';
import { validate } from 'avss-lite-Raka503';

const userSchema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(2),
  email: z.string().email(),
});

const result = validate(userSchema, {
  name: 'Rakha',
  email: 'rakha@example.com',
});

if (result.success) {
  console.log(result.data);
} else {
  console.error(result.errors);
}`" />
  </section>

  <section id="quick-start-security" class="quick-start-section">
    <h2>5. Initialize security</h2>
    <p>
      Create a SecurityFramework instance. The framework exposes
      CSRF, XSS, security headers, CORS, cookies, proxy, and rate-limit utilities.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock language="typescript" :code="`import { createSecurity } from 'avss-lite-Raka503';

const security = createSecurity();

console.log(security.csrf);
console.log(security.xss);
console.log(security.headers);
console.log(security.cors);
console.log(security.cookies);
console.log(security.proxy);
console.log(security.rateLimit);`" />
  </section>

  <section id="quick-start-logger" class="quick-start-section">
    <h2>6. Log application events</h2>
    <p>Use the built-in logger singleton.</p>
    <CodeBlock language="typescript" :code="`import { logger } from 'avss-lite-Raka503';

logger.info('Application started');
logger.success('Operation completed');
logger.security('Security event detected');
logger.database('Database operation executed');
logger.error('Unexpected error occurred');`" />
  </section>

  <section id="quick-start-run" class="quick-start-section">
    <h2>7. Run your application</h2>
    <CodeBlock language="bash" :code="'bun run src/index.ts'" />
    <p>Verify the output in your terminal.</p>
